I'm sorry,  but if I understood you correctly,  you believe that Biden speaks eloquently.  This leads me to wonder what speeches you've listened to in comparison with his speeches that I've heard.  Reason being,  I've heard his unprofessional outbursts,  as well as his very unprofessional name calling in reference to not just Putin, but also the Crown Price of Saudi Arabia.  The way he speaks about other world leaders is far from being eloquent,  also don't forget some of his best speeches were stolen from other speakers like Jfk And someone else,   ican't recall at the moment.  and quite frankly, I would even venture to say that could be language considered as incitful. Or provocative at the very least.  We don't need a President provoking leaders of nations that we already have existing tension.  Furthermore,  in regards to the current Israeli,  Palestinian conflict our eloquent President can't seem to make a firm abs clear stance.  On one hand he says we back Israel 100%, he sends money and weapons to assist with the war Isreal is waging,  however at the same time he publicly criticisizes the way that Israel is conducting its war, or response to Hamas aggression.  However you want to view it.  Personally,  I see it as an active war to rid the Gaza strip of its current occupation, to include the Palestinian civilians.  It appears that the ultimate goal is to have a land that has no living people and is in total ruin, but that's just my opinion that I've formed from watching the actions of the Israeli government.  Either way the point is my so called eloquently speaking President hasn't taken a clear stance,  in fact it appears he's confused about his stance.  If we had Israel's back 100% he wouldn't publicly Critique the Israeli leader's method of response,  because this does not look like he's 100% behind Israel.. what it looks like is that he's sending help because he feels he's obligated to do so, but that, like every other nation, he doesn't agree with the brutality.  Or perhaps he doesn't really care about innocent people being murdered, he's just saying that to look good.  Because the fact that US continues to veto every cease fire motion in the UN, and considering that Biden continues to fight for more aide to be sent to Israel in weapons and money looks more like he couldn't care less who dies.  To have a clear stance is to not make public criticism,  and continue sending weapons and money.  To take a clear stance that proves he genuinely cares about innocent Palestinian people being murdered would require him to distance himself, and this country from Israel, as well as end any and all aide to Israel from the US, AND stand with other countries order to cease fire at UN  Charter assembly..
Case and point,  from where I'm standing there's nothing clear, or eloquent about Joe Biden,  I feel your indifference or hatred of Trump clouds your ability to judge Biden logically.  You can hate Trump, that's fine,  I can understand why many people do hate him, he doesn't mince words,  he tweets like a school boy when he's a leader,  I have my qualms with Trump as well,  I don't let my disgust with Biden cloud my ability to see Trump logically.  However,  it appears thru this interview and considering the illogical mindset of everyone else that hates Trump that the collective hatred of Trump has impaired the minds of people to such a degree that you're all no longer able to soundly judge anyone else.  And the more rights of Americans that are being threatened by Trump haters, the more clear it becomes that People who hate Trump have become so consumed with hating Trump that they've injured their own ability to use critical thinking when they look at Biden.   For the damn record,  if you all Hate Trump so damn much,  then why not consider RFK JR at least,  instead of screwing the entire country for another 4 years by choosing a man who clearly HATES THE AMERICAN PEOPLE AND CAN'T TELL HIS OWN BUTT HOLE FROM A HOLE IN THE GROUND..

